% Probe: how far below the baseline an inline-math SUBSCRIPT sits, and what
% that does to the line advance.
%
% This is what is left of the enumitem manual's back-half divergence once the
% pagination fixes are in. On its page 17 (a run of `+item{${m_{J*}...}}`
% lines) the port advances 23.30-24.50pt per item where upstream advances
% 21.49-21.74pt, and inside each item the subscript row sits +4.728pt below its
% own base row where upstream puts it +2.964pt — read out of the CONTENT
% STREAM with `scripts/vspace_probe/baselines.py`, not from `pdftotext -bbox`
% (the two writers' math descriptors differ).
%
% ~12 such lines accumulate ~25pt over one page, which is why the port's
% page 17 ends one `+code` block earlier than upstream's. The pagination is
% not what is wrong there; the math box's depth is.
%
% Rows 1-3 vary one thing each so the two effects can be separated:
%   1. plain CJK        — the control, must agree exactly
%   2. subscript only   — the script drop
%   3. sub + superscript — whether the height moves too
@require: stdjabook
@require: math

document (|
  title = {math script drop probe};
  author = {};
  show-title = false;
  show-toc = false;
|) '<
  +p{あいうえお。}
  +p{かきくけこ${m_{J}}さしすせそ。}
  +p{たちつてと${m_{J}^{*}}なにぬねの。}
  +p{はひふへほ。}
>
